  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/tests/adaptive_troch_parallel.rs`: `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes` has the ignore reason `heavy lane: ...`. The release tier and `cargo xtask gate heavy` run it with `--ignored` in the step `motion heavy: adaptive_troch_parallel`. The test keeps its two pockets (30x24 D6, 44x36 D10), all its shape asserts and its 90 s budget. The budget is now a guard on the release run.\n- New light twin `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes_light` (`light lane: ...`). It checks the 30x24 D6 pocket only, in release.\n- `docs/decisions/3141-parallel-lane-heavy.md` records the decision. It replaces the rule \"apply the budget in every run\" of decision #2990 for this test.\n\n## Why\n\nThe debug test took 36, 64, 106, 140 and 145 s on unchanged motion code (#3116, #3141). The red runs were on a loaded post-merge runner. Wall time on a loaded runner is not a function of the code. AGENTS.md \"Testing\" moves a test above about 60 s in debug to the heavy lane.\n\nDropped: a larger debug budget (any number can fail under load); a smaller fixture (decision #2990 measured that a 38x33 D10 pocket fails the rest-area assert, and a smaller pocket weakens the 32.36 mm case).\n\n## Readings (local, at 2c2b4bcbb, CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0, -j 18)\n\n- Release, `--ignored --exact`: `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes` ok in 15.72 s (budget 90 s).\n- Release, `--ignored --exact`: `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes_light` ok in 7.58 s.\n- Debug, `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test adaptive_troch_parallel`: 1 passed (`corner_cleanup_reduces_34x16_rest_to_at_most_hsm_rest`, 28.81 s), 2 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes` (heavy lane)\n- `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes_light` (light lane)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy` and `cargo xtask gate light` were not run as gate commands. The same tests ran with direct cargo calls in release.\n- The batch gate on the post-merge runner.\n\nThe `#[test]` count of the binary goes from 2 to 3 (the light twin). No test was removed.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium (issue label effort:low; not escalated)\n\nFixes #3141\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
